{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/319291-inspirational-sources-for-promethean","id":319291,"title":"Inspirational Sources for Promethean","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-22T14:03:29-08:00","id":319291,"title":"Inspirational Sources for Promethean","content":"So I recently picked up Kingdom Hearts 358/2 Days for the DS, and I gotta say I'm finding my old impressions about Nobodies being dead ringers for Prometheans is dead on. Roxas's exploration on what people do, what emotions are, and struggling over his lack of a heart(even though that's a lie) and worldly understanding is wonderfully explored through the game and the side material of his diary entries. The Organization on the whole feels like an extremely dangerous throng that sometimes asks a lot of questions about humanity in some really harsh ways, with Xemnas being almost perfect Centimani material. Xion herself is a dead ringer for a particular Lineage(I won't spoil, since people care about that sort of thing). It's just a very good look into a group of people who have all the power in the world, and what drives them to claim humanity in spite of that.<br /> <br /> So, since I had that, I figured I'd ask-what do you go to for Promethean material?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T15:12:34-08:00","id":319400,"title":"","content":"I know it's probably mentioned in the book, but the Original Frankenstein is a must read, if only to disabuse people of the idea it's the same as the Hammer Horror rendition. &quot;Adam&quot;(for lack of a better name)'s struggle to just interact with people seems to fit quite well, not to mention all the ways it inspired mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T15:25:40-08:00","id":319439,"title":"","content":"Though it's far from a perfect fit (on account of having an actual birth family, among other things) and could just be owed to my loving the concept in general, I feel like the arc of Koto the Younger from <i>Kyousougiga</i> bears some thematic suitability, as does the story's broader themes of renewal and destruction.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Seeing unmistakable signs that your attempt to connect with your long-lost family may have <i>destroyed their world</i> and being locked into wordlessly going about definitely finishing the process shortly after the revelation that <i>you were an accident</i> are the kind of things that make you think about this; Inari's self-loathing and despairing of his contradictory purposes does likewise, but he's explicitly a god in a story set in a time where the boundary between god and man was vague.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T16:46:12-08:00","id":319498,"title":"","content":"The current season of American Horror Story has some great input, though, as always, it's not great t.v. It's about a freak show, naturally, and the Halloween two-parter features some main characters sharing their worst dealings with normal people.<br /> <br /> Musically, &quot;Nada&quot; by the Refreshments is particular thematic. &quot;I've been away from the living, I/don't need to be forgiven, I/ am just waiting for this cold, hard sun-cracked soul of mine/ to come alive&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-22T19:47:06-08:00","id":319569,"title":"","content":"I just saw a showing of <i>Little Shop of Horrors</i>... andit catches some of the notes <i>perfectly</i>.<br /> <br /> &quot;Somewhere That's Green&quot; is really Promethean in sentiment (paraphrased: &quot;oh god, I want to live in a suburb where everything is nice and clean and the same and where my boyfriend <i>doesn't hurt me.</i> Where I can be a normal person, instead of an unlovable wretch who deserves abuse.&quot;), as are a few lines (&quot;he took me in as a little tyke. He gave me a warm place to sleep under the counter, fed me nice things like meatloaf and water, and I get <i>every second Sunday</i> off!&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T04:58:54-08:00","id":319807,"title":"","content":"<b>Full Metal Alchmist</b>, espcieally first anime series - with Alphosen Elric, boy's soul trapped in the body of metal armor - is great inspiration for the Constructs as whole in the game.<br /> <br /> With addition of &quot;Nemo&quot; song of Nightwish, that is great for general Promethean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nemo lyrics</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is me for forever<br /> One of the lost ones<br /> The one without a name<br /> Without an honest heart as compass<br /> This is me for forever<br /> One without a name<br /> These lines the last endeavor<br /> To find the missing lifeline<br /> <br /> Oh how I wish<br /> For soothing rain<br /> All I wish is to dream again<br /> My loving heart<br /> Lost in the dark<br /> For hope I'd give my everything(...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Below you got both with this delisious AMV for Created.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/pKCqaUSXaO4\" data-code=\"pKCqaUSXaO4\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/pKCqaUSXaO4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T02:45:51-08:00","id":321606,"title":"","content":"Metamorphosis by Kafka kind of fits with disquiet and how it can build up even in people you think you can trust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3707-thediabadass","name":"TheDiabadass","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T11:21:25-08:00","id":321989,"title":"","content":"&quot;May,&quot; a delightful little movie I've talked about on the forums before. Highly recommended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T08:19:37-08:00","id":326022,"title":"","content":"I say it every time, but in addition to <i>May</i> (good call, Ben Quo), <i>Dirty Pretty Things </i>is my go-to inspiration for <b>Promethean</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T08:48:02-08:00","id":326058,"title":"","content":"I can't remember the name of the movie but its about a lone woman moving to a remote town and having to do whatever the towns people say to stay there. Gets pretty horrific.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T09:24:58-08:00","id":326090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/319291-inspirational-sources-for-promethean?p=326058#post326058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't remember the name of the movie but its about a lone woman moving to a remote town and having to do whatever the towns people say to stay there. Gets pretty horrific.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Dogville&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T05:10:29-08:00","id":326853,"title":"","content":"Oh, yeah, <i>Dogville</i>. Brutal movie, very appropriate for <b>Promethean</b>. <br /> <br /> And then, of course, there's <i>I, Frankenstein</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T05:36:53-08:00","id":326866,"title":"","content":"Penny Dreadful has a cool example of a place a Promethean might fit in for a while, as well as how suddenly and irretrievably he can fuck it up. (The Creature's arc in the first season could serve as a good example of find a Role, learn the right lesson, stay too long because it's comfortable, step outside, and have everything go to hell). Add in a newborn Promethean imagery, and multiple shades of creation/creator relationships.<br /> <br /> Also, it gets some hella bleak shots of the Thames, a total Wasteland vibe (though it's mostly another character's arc they relate to).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T05:43:20-08:00","id":326869,"title":"","content":"At this point, I'd like to recommend the early Grant Morrison graphic novel <i>The Mystery Play</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4413-frances-best-friend","name":"Frances' Best Friend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4413_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T08:35:44-08:00","id":327028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/319291-inspirational-sources-for-promethean?p=326853#post326853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And then, of course, there's <i>I, Frankenstein</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I wouldn't have pegged that one in particular, thematically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T09:09:35-08:00","id":327110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/319291-inspirational-sources-for-promethean?p=326853#post326853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, yeah, <i>Dogville</i>. Brutal movie, very appropriate for <b>Promethean</b>. <br /> <br /> And then, of course, there's <i>I, Frankenstein</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, looked up Dogville. A very appropriate and very DISTURBING looking into a Tammuz's Disquiet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T13:58:59-08:00","id":327361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/319291-inspirational-sources-for-promethean?p=327028#post327028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I wouldn't have pegged that one in particular, thematically.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, it's not, and it's terrible movie, besides. I was just kidding around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T22:58:09-08:00","id":327898,"title":"","content":"I looked up &quot;Dogville.&quot;<br /> Can I just add that every Lars von Trier movie I have ever seen reminded me of intense, intense Disquiet/Torment? (and in the case of &quot;Antichrist,&quot; a Riven Wasteland?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T08:43:59-08:00","id":328259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/319291-inspirational-sources-for-promethean?p=327110#post327110\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, looked up Dogville. A very appropriate and very DISTURBING looking into a Tammuz's Disquiet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting I always looked at it as Galateid disquiet. However, I can totally see it as a Tammuz diquiet effect as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T08:58:34-08:00","id":328266,"title":"","content":"I will always recommend the 1970s era <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0077031/?ref_=nv_sr_3\" target=\"_blank\">Incredible Hulk TV series</a> with Bill Bixby as a source for <b>Promethean</b>.<br /> <br /> Always traveling? Check.<br /> Always persecuted wherever he goes? Check.<br /> Always freaks out and goes brutal on the people? Check.<br /> Always trying to change his condition? Check.<br /> Can't tell anyone what he really is? Check.<br /> Only the most level-headed and kindest people will not freak out at the sight of him? Check.<br /> <br /> I believe that my love of that show is directly tied to my love of this game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T10:17:03-08:00","id":328367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/319291-inspirational-sources-for-promethean?p=328266#post328266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will always recommend the 1970s era <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0077031/?ref_=nv_sr_3\" target=\"_blank\">Incredible Hulk TV series</a> with Bill Bixby as a source for <b>Promethean</b>.<br /> <br /> Always traveling? Check.<br /> Always persecuted wherever he goes? Check.<br /> Always freaks out and goes brutal on the people? Check.<br /> Always trying to change his condition? Check.<br /> Can't tell anyone what he really is? Check.<br /> Only the most level-headed and kindest people will not freak out at the sight of him? Check.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, that is a really good comparison. Never would have pegged a 70's TV show for a source of inspiration for Promethean, but there it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-02T10:58:19-08:00","id":328439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/319291-inspirational-sources-for-promethean?p=328367#post328367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, that is a really good comparison. Never would have pegged a 70's TV show for a source of inspiration for Promethean, but there it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, and it's not like it's a vague comparison, either. The default character arc of a Promethean from Creation to New Dawn is nearly identical to the entire premise of the show. The way he kept trying multiple techniques to deal with the problem? There's your Refinements. There was even an episode where he tried to rid himself of his curse by passing it off to someone else, i.e. needing to make another Promethean as a milestone for the New Dawn.<br /> <br /> Arguably, several of the &quot;wandering hero&quot; shows from that same era could be applied, but none of them had the protagonist turning into a monster like that. Well, <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0092480/?ref_=fn_al_tt_3\" target=\"_blank\">except this one</a>, but it didn't do well and it crosses established game lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T05:51:03-08:00","id":331012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/319291-inspirational-sources-for-promethean?p=328439#post328439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup, and it's not like it's a vague comparison, either. The default character arc of a Promethean from Creation to New Dawn is nearly identical to the entire premise of the show. The way he kept trying multiple techniques to deal with the problem? There's your Refinements. There was even an episode where he tried to rid himself of his curse by passing it off to someone else, i.e. needing to make another Promethean as a milestone for the New Dawn.<br /> <br /> Arguably, several of the &quot;wandering hero&quot; shows from that same era could be applied, but none of them had the protagonist turning into a monster like that. Well, <a href=\"http://www.imdb.com/title/tt0092480/?ref_=fn_al_tt_3\" target=\"_blank\">except this one</a>, but it didn't do well and it crosses established game lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if I ever have the pleasure of running a Promethean game, I'll be able to grab those DVDs off of my shelf and show my players before starting. Fantastic comparison sir.<br /> <br /> Sticking with the recent topic on the Rivers of the Dead, could you also draw a parallel to the episode where he gets paralyzed to a Promethean's single &quot;Death Cycle&quot;? I think you could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":1923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","user":"BigDamnHero","date":". 12-05-2014, 08:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T05:59:10-08:00","id":331014,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think that &quot;The Golem &amp; the Jinni&quot; is a great inspiration for Promethean- or, more exactly, a promethean/demon crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T06:43:27-08:00","id":331040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/319291-inspirational-sources-for-promethean?p=331012#post331012\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sticking with the recent topic on the Rivers of the Dead, could you also draw a parallel to the episode where he gets paralyzed to a Promethean's single &quot;Death Cycle&quot;? I think you could.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember that specific episode well enough to make the call, but I'm sure it wouldn't be tough to draw the lines of comparison considering how much else fits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T06:54:06-08:00","id":331044,"title":"","content":"I've recently rewatched Trigun and thought it could be seen as a Promethean pilgrimage and his quest to try to bring back his Centimany sibling back to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-05T10:04:23-08:00","id":331250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/319291-inspirational-sources-for-promethean?p=331044#post331044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've recently rewatched Trigun and thought it could be seen as a Promethean pilgrimage and his quest to try to bring back his Centimany sibling back to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually genius.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T05:21:46-08:00","id":332160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/319291-inspirational-sources-for-promethean?p=331044#post331044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've recently rewatched Trigun and thought it could be seen as a Promethean pilgrimage and his quest to try to bring back his Centimany sibling back to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I would have never thought of that one myself. It is however really fitting.<br /> <br /> The TV series certainly has elements of it. The Manga definitely has a lot of more Promethean style themes revolving around &quot;The Plants&quot;. The Gun Ho Guns also make a pretty good collection of &quot;weird stuff&quot; from around the WoD. Knives is indeed a pretty awesome example of the Hundred Handed too.<br /> <br /> As Arts said genius good sir.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-06T20:19:30-08:00","id":332708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/319291-inspirational-sources-for-promethean?p=327898#post327898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I looked up &quot;Dogville.&quot;<br /> Can I just add that every Lars von Trier movie I have ever seen reminded me of intense, intense Disquiet/Torment? (and in the case of &quot;Antichrist,&quot; a Riven Wasteland?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Lars von Triers' <i>The Idiots </i>is...a movie. I can't honestly recommend it, partially because the subject matter is so patently ugly and offensive, and partially because I intrinsically dislike the Dogme 95 art movement, but it sometimes seems like it was a film made about Prometheans, <i>by</i> a Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T01:41:07-08:00","id":334921,"title":"","content":"Much like Wyrdhamster, I like looking at <i>Fullmetal Alchemist: Brotherhood</i> and its homunculi for ideas about prometheans and their capabilities...<br /> <br /> But--and I'm surprised no one has mentioned this--but there's a game that was developed by Capcom that serves not only as a great inspiration for the first edition of <i>Promethean</i>, but I believe also would serve as an excellent source of ideas for the second edition coming out (not just for characters, but also for settings and storyteller ideas).<br /> <br /> The game is called <i>Haunting Ground</i>, and follows the story of a young girl called Fiona who gets stranded at a large castle occupied by a number of occupants wishing to do her harm. Why you ask? Because despite being completely human she possesses an Azoth, which pretty much all the characters in the castle wish to utilize in some fashion (save for one)--<br /> <br /> Besides any number of deformed homunculi stranded throughout the castle, along with a few golems you have to take control of, and a list of references to alchemical procedures and famous alchemists throughout history--you have to contend with the stalkers of the game. Two characters are dead ringers for prometheans, both of which were created by alchemical means in-game--one, named Debilitas, is a superlatively strong yet mentally deficient man; and two, Daniella, a mentally unstable woman of unearthly beauty who lacks any sense of touch, taste, and smell. <br /> <br /> Then two other characters are dead ringers for the antagonists in the second edition coming up (Alchemists)--Lorenzo, the aging alchemist who's behind all the workings at the castle; and Riccardo, Lorenzo's clone. Both characters want to use Fiona's Azoth in order to gain immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-17T11:47:20-08:00","id":343127,"title":"","content":"naoki urasawa's monster","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4554-ndisi-the-king","name":"ndisi the king","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T13:37:26-08:00","id":347647,"title":"","content":"I just watched <i>Terry Pratchett's Hogfather</i> DVD the other night (a holiday tradition for us), and the depiction of Death was very <b>Promethean</b> in terms of being someone who quite loves humanity but just cannot QUITE be one regardless of how much he tries. It's very clear analog to the Refinement of Gold. The book adds depth to this, and the approach in other novels like <i>Mort</i> and <i>Reaperman</i> do as well, offering looks into possible expressions of Cuprum and maybe Stannum, respectively.<br /> <br /> Heck, now that I think about it, there's a LOT of appropriate themes throughout the Discworld novels. The character of Susan Sto Helit looks human but can't ever shake the touch of her grandfather's realm. <i>Feat of Clay</i> and subsequent stories about golems provide natural paralels. Even <i>The Last Hero</i> shows some hints at what a transformative pilgrimage might look like...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-22T17:41:37-08:00","id":347878,"title":"","content":"Edward Scissorhands strikes me as a good one. It is a particularly good illustration of the gradual progression of Disquiet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T05:00:46-08:00","id":348188,"title":"","content":"I may be alone on this, but I think Dark Souls works. Not only does it have the same sad atmosphere and cool/bizarre monsters, but you actually play as an undead that can acquire humanity, though in a different way from Promethean. The system for covenants, leaving behind messages and cooperating in multiplayer can also give inspiration for how your Prommie approaches his Refinement and how Throngs may help/hinder each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T23:08:47-08:00","id":349609,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of funky folk and fairy tales get overlooked for Promethean. The <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Steam_Man_of_the_Prairies\" target=\"_blank\">Steam Man of the Plains</a>, for one. The Velveteen Rabbit for another (it even has a big cleansing fire metaphor at the end).<br /> <br /> Even Frosty the Snowman has a weird riff on the Golem myth; instead of removing a letter on his forehead, it's the removing of his hat that deactivates him. He also has a fairly Disquieted fellow pursuing him, and even helps build his own wife with the help of his troupe of Demiurges.<br /> <br /> Finally, let us all remember Elbis O'Shaughnessey in the final volume of <i>Sandman</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","user":"Metamurpho","date":".  Plains not planes! 12-26-2014, 12:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T19:56:20-08:00","id":374739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/319291-inspirational-sources-for-promethean?p=349609#post349609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Frosty the Snowman has a weird riff on the Golem myth</div> </div> </div> </div>In a similar vein, there's the Gingerbread Man. His disquiet causes people to want to eat him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-18-2015, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T20:10:41-08:00","id":374753,"title":"","content":"No matter how hard I try, all of my group's attempts at Promethean end up as <i>Rocky Horror Picture Show </i>meets <i>Young Frankenstein</i>, with a dash of <i>Weird Science.</i><br /> <br /> That said, you could totally make a case for Rocky as a Galateid and Frank-N-Furter as his crazed demierge. Not entirely sure how you write Riff-Raff; perhaps a bizarre <i>qashmallim</i> tasked with driving Rocky away from his creator?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T12:18:32-08:00","id":384396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/319291-inspirational-sources-for-promethean?p=374753#post374753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No matter how hard I try, all of my group's attempts at Promethean end up as <i>Rocky Horror Picture Show </i>meets <i>Young Frankenstein</i>, with a dash of <i>Weird Science.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>And you're complaining?<br /> <br /> Invite me over next time. I'll be Eddie (Meatloaf for dinner again?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T03:40:54-08:00","id":384896,"title":"","content":"When I was writing Tammuz, the life of Tommy Wiseau (the guy that made The Room) came to mind. Pick up the Disaster Artist by Greg Sestero and tell me he doesn't sound like a Prommie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I had a signature but now I don't but it won't let me leave this blank so yeah.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/199-yue","name":"Yue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar199_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T19:10:26-07:00","id":925168,"title":"","content":"Feathertop by Nathaniel Hawthorne is about a scarecrow brought to life by a witch. The Oz books by L. Frank Baum with the Scarecrow, Tin man, Jack Pumpkinhead, etcetera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T11:31:37-07:00","id":925427,"title":"","content":"Marvel's current <i>Vision</i> ongoing is one hundred percent fire, in addition to being a gold mine of excellent Promethean material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T13:10:18-07:00","id":925475,"title":"","content":"I'm going to throw down iZombie the comic book. It has three Created, a mummy, a coterie of vampires, and as you may have guessed, zombies. Plus were-terriers, talking chimps, and off-brand Cthulhu. It's not like, &quot;Oh my god, that is <i>sooo</i> Promethean,&quot; but it hits a lot of the right notes. The protagonist is amnesiac, created with a purpose, and transcends her condition at the end of it all. I'd recommend the tv show as well, but not for the same reasons (if you're a <i>Veronica Mars</i> fan with a love of corny gags, your should definitely watch it).<br /> <br /> Also, <i>Orphan Black</i>. This one is a bit trippier, and probably further off the mark, but if you're the sort who does grapple with Promethean transhumanism, <i>Orphan Black</i> might be your girl. First, I'm going to recommend it just on Tatiana Maslany's incredible performances. You will forget that Sarah, Alison, et al., are being played by the same actress; you could take that feat of thespianism as an inspiration for how a given Promethean might approach each Role as an opportunity to try on a whole new personality. There is the overall conspiracy of Neolutionism, with its mad science, its underground counterculture, and its zealous opposition in the Proletheans, and the question they all raise is what is the place of the artificial person? It's probably also great inspiration for Demon and Deviant (presumably). There's also a distinct love for real, actual science and research, and while it's not always accurate, there's never a fast technobabble solution to anything.<br /> <br /> Maybe <i>Humans</i>? I kinda liked it, but never made it past the first couple of episodes. The new <i>WestWorld</i> looks like it's going to be told from the robots' point of view, which straight up Promethean, plus it's Jonathn Nolan, who's behind <i>Person of Interest</i>, which is anti-Promethean in that the demiurge here is trying to shepherd his incredible creation into a responsible adulthood. And <i>always</i> The Incredible Hulk, and to a lesser degree, Kung Fu Theater and The Fugitive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T10:24:41-07:00","id":926490,"title":"","content":"Surprised I never put this here, but Simon Dark by Steve Niles and Scott Hampton. A literal Created on a journey of revenge (sort of) and self understanding.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Simon-Dark-VOL-Steve-Niles/dp/1401218490\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Simon-Dark-VOL-Steve-Niles/dp/1401218490\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Simon-Dark-VOL-Steve-Niles/dp/1401218490\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.amazon.com/Simon-Dark-VOL-Steve-Niles/dp/1401218490 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T09:21:52-07:00","id":930898,"title":"","content":"Really great suggestions here. I'd add the PC game Planescape: Torment for tone and theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T22:10:24-07:00","id":932405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/319291-inspirational-sources-for-promethean?p=384896#post384896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I was writing Tammuz, the life of Tommy Wiseau (the guy that made The Room) came to mind. Pick up the Disaster Artist by Greg Sestero and tell me he doesn't sound like a Prommie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of people who seem like Prometheans, I was going to mention Dr. Steve Brule as an Aurum follower. <br /> <br /> Let's see, a lot of the good stuff about robots can be applied to Promethean. I'm someone who's against the focus on becoming human, so that prejudice might be evident here, but that doesn't mean I can't recognize a good narrative about a created being. Back to robots, Metropolis is an early one. Asimov's robot stories are also amazing. To me, they're almost like an ultimately more hopeful continuation of Frankenstein, since they posit that artificial life forms aren't necessarily destined to always turn against their creators. <br /> <br /> Young Frankenstein, in addition to being hilarious, is one of the few adaptations of the original that doesn't twist it into some sort of anti-science parable. <br /> <br /> I've always had a weird crossover headcanon that in the ChroD universe cyborg ninja Raiden would actually be a Promethean made from the corpse of the actual Raiden. He's interesting in that he comes very close to returning completely to being human, only to give it up when he decides that there are threats to humanity he needs to keep fighting. <br /> <br /> Musically, Janelle Monae and The Protomen are both great as sources of inspiration for Promethean. Again, anything good about robots can be about Prometheans if you want it to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T19:48:57-07:00","id":932744,"title":"","content":"Highly recommend the books <i>Perfected</i> and <i>Tarnished </i>by Kate Jarvik Birch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T18:30:31-07:00","id":934227,"title":"","content":"You know for some strange reason a voice in the back of my is screaming Waiting For Godot as good material, but I think I'd need to re-read it to be sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T11:04:08-07:00","id":935690,"title":"","content":"